From fca3ae3604abae4ab677171332022e696638c588 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:08:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(od-sevev): palette v3, the chrome in Israel's blue
 and white

Bar: "the design should be more in Israel's palette, with blue and white".
- palette.py v3: the plum/violet chrome darks re-valued into a navy family
  around the flag blue, ids kept (night, plum, plum_hi, ui_scrim, ui_panel,
  ui_bubble, ui_bub_hi); new ui_mute and ui_rule. night/plum/plum_hi move in
  the creative pack's palette too, so Balfour's sky is navy and the curtain
  (title, OG, icon) is velvet blue.
- Kit (255 pieces, same ids and sizes): sheet_modal title band in flag blue
  with a white stripe; white-over-flag stripes on the tab bar, the ticker
  (was red) and the chat header; pink accents (spin stripe, spins tab arcs,
  slot G arcs, the s14 play glyph) moved to the blue family.
- Stages: stage_balfour (sky) and stage_washington (a 1-row rule) re-rendered
  into the approved out/; a full render reports 0 drift, the cast untouched.
- The fork letter palette (art/sprites.ts -> art.json): grape, violet,
  lavender and pink letters moved to navy / flag / sky; content.json's
  Balfour skyBands follow. Pipeline re-import with --godot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
